('t4-mcq-01', 4, '4.1.4', 'A', 'mcq', 1, 'A country''s index of export prices rises to 110 and its index of import prices rises to 125 (base year = 100 for both). What is its terms of trade index?', null, '["A 113.6","B 115.0","C 88.0","D 85.0"]'::jsonb),
('t4-mcq-02', 4, '4.1.2', 'A', 'mcq', 1, 'In Country X, one worker can produce either 10 metres of cloth or 5 tonnes of wheat. In Country Y, one worker can produce either 6 metres of cloth or 4 tonnes of wheat. Which statement is correct?', null, '["A Country X has a comparative advantage in both goods.","B Country X has a comparative advantage in cloth and Country Y in wheat.","C Country Y has a comparative advantage in cloth and Country X in wheat.","D Neither country can gain from trade because Country X has an absolute advantage in both goods."]'::jsonb),
('t4-mcq-03', 4, '4.1.5', 'A', 'mcq', 1, 'Which feature distinguishes a customs union from a free trade area?', null, '["A The removal of tariffs on trade between members","B A single currency used by all members","C Free movement of labour between members","D A common external tariff on imports from non-members"]'::jsonb),
('t4-mcq-04', 4, '4.1.6', 'A', 'mcq', 1, 'A country imposes a tariff of £2 per tonne on imported steel. Before the tariff, imports were 600,000 tonnes a year. After the tariff, domestic production rises, domestic consumption falls and imports fall to 300,000 tonnes a year. Assuming the world price is unchanged, what is the government''s annual tariff revenue?', null, '["A £600,000","B £1,200,000","C £300,000","D £900,000"]'::jsonb),
('t4-mcq-05', 4, '4.1.7', 'A', 'mcq', 1, 'A UK car company builds a new factory in Mexico. How is this recorded in the UK balance of payments?', null, '["A As a debit in trade in goods in the current account","B As outward foreign direct investment in the financial account","C As a credit in primary income in the current account","D As a debit in secondary income in the current account"]'::jsonb),
('t4-mcq-06', 4, '4.1.8', 'A', 'mcq', 1, 'The exchange rate changes from £1 = $1.25 to £1 = $1.40. A UK-made product is priced at £200 and its sterling price is unchanged. What is the percentage change in its US dollar price?', null, '["A +12%","B -10.7%","C +15%","D +30%"]'::jsonb),
('t4-mcq-07', 4, '4.1.8', 'A', 'mcq', 1, 'According to the Marshall-Lerner condition, a depreciation of a country''s currency will improve its current account balance if', null, '["A the price elasticity of demand for exports is greater than 1.","B the country already has a current account surplus.","C the sum of the price elasticities of demand for exports and imports (ignoring signs) is greater than 1.","D the price elasticity of demand for imports is less than 1."]'::jsonb),
('t4-mcq-08', 4, '4.1.9', 'A', 'mcq', 1, 'Which of the following is most likely to improve the UK''s international competitiveness?', null, '["A Labour productivity grows more slowly than wages.","B Sterling appreciates against major currencies.","C UK relative unit labour costs fall compared with those of trading partners.","D UK corporation tax rises relative to that of other countries."]'::jsonb),
('t4-mcq-09', 4, '4.2.1', 'A', 'mcq', 1, 'In the UK, a household is commonly regarded as being in relative poverty if its income is', null, '["A insufficient to buy the basic necessities of food, shelter and clothing.","B below 50% of mean household income.","C below the level of the National Living Wage.","D below 60% of median household income."]'::jsonb),
('t4-mcq-10', 4, '4.2.2', 'A', 'mcq', 1, 'On a Lorenz curve diagram, the area between the line of perfect equality and the Lorenz curve is 0.15, and the area beneath the Lorenz curve is 0.35. What is the Gini coefficient?', null, '["A 0.15","B 0.30","C 0.43","D 0.50"]'::jsonb),
('t4-mcq-11', 4, '4.3.1', 'A', 'mcq', 1, 'Which set of indicators is used to construct the Human Development Index (HDI)?', null, '["A Life expectancy at birth, mean and expected years of schooling, and GNI per capita at purchasing power parity","B Real GDP growth, inflation and unemployment","C Infant mortality, adult literacy and the Gini coefficient","D GNI per capita, access to clean water and carbon emissions per capita"]'::jsonb),
('t4-mcq-12', 4, '4.3.2', 'A', 'mcq', 1, 'Why might dependence on exports of a single primary product limit economic growth in a developing economy?', null, '["A Primary products have a high income elasticity of demand, so world demand rises faster than world income.","B Primary products are subject to tariffs in every developed country.","C Primary product industries are unable to attract foreign direct investment.","D Primary product prices tend to be volatile because demand and supply are price inelastic, making export earnings and tax revenue unpredictable."]'::jsonb),
('t4-mcq-13', 4, '4.4.3', 'A', 'mcq', 1, 'Which of the following describes the role of a central bank as ''lender of last resort''?', null, '["A Lending to the government at zero interest to finance its budget deficit","B Providing emergency liquidity to commercial banks that face a temporary shortage of funds","C Lending directly to households who are unable to obtain mortgages","D Guaranteeing every deposit held in commercial banks without limit"]'::jsonb),
('t4-mcq-14', 4, '4.5.2', 'A', 'mcq', 1, 'Under an illustrative income tax system, the first £12,000 of income is tax-free, income from £12,001 to £50,000 is taxed at 20%, and income above £50,000 is taxed at 40%. What is the average rate of income tax paid by someone earning £60,000?', null, '["A 40.0%","B 20.0%","C 19.3%","D 26.7%"]'::jsonb),
('t4-mcq-15', 4, '4.5.3', 'A', 'mcq', 1, 'Which of the following best describes a cyclical budget deficit?', null, '["A The part of the deficit caused by the economy operating below trend output, as tax revenues fall and welfare spending rises automatically","B A deficit that would remain even if the economy were operating at its trend level of output","C The total stock of government debt accumulated over time","D A deficit caused by government spending on capital investment"]'::jsonb),
