('t4-data-01a', 4, '4.1.4', 'A', 'data', 5, 'Using Table 1, calculate Kanara''s terms of trade index for 2015 and 2025 (2020 = 100), and explain the significance of the change.', 'Kanara: a commodity-dependent economy (illustrative data)

Kanara is a fictional lower-middle-income country in sub-Saharan Africa with a population of 24 million.

Table 1: Selected indicators for Kanara (illustrative data)
Indicator | 2015 | 2020 | 2025
GDP per capita (US$, PPP) | 3,400 | 3,900 | 4,100
Human Development Index | 0.52 | 0.55 | 0.56
Cocoa and copper as % of export earnings | 68 | 74 | 77
Index of export prices (2020 = 100) | 112 | 100 | 92
Index of import prices (2020 = 100) | 94 | 100 | 115
Net inflows of foreign direct investment (US$ billion) | 0.6 | 1.4 | 2.1
Population below the international extreme poverty line (%) | 41 | 36 | 35

Extract A: Cocoa, copper and constraints
Most of Kanara''s workforce is employed in small-scale farming, where cocoa yields are low because farmers lack access to credit for fertiliser and improved seedlings. Copper mining is dominated by two foreign multinational companies, which have increased investment since a 2019 law cut mining royalty rates. The mines employ relatively few local workers and import most of their machinery. Government revenue fell sharply in 2024 when world copper prices dropped, forcing cuts to spending on rural schools and roads. Corruption in the allocation of mining licences remains a concern, and around 30% of the population lacks access to electricity.

Extract B: Two development plans
Kanara''s government is considering two approaches. A finance ministry plan would cut tariffs on manufactured imports, privatise the state electricity company and offer tax breaks to attract more foreign investment. An alternative plan, backed by some development organisations, would save part of mining revenues in a sovereign wealth fund, invest in rural infrastructure and education, and support farmer co-operatives to process cocoa into chocolate products locally rather than exporting raw beans.', null),
